# AI-TP Global Conventions

- Keep current layering: `backend/api/routes` (HTTP), `backend/services` (business logic), `backend/models` + `backend/schemas` (data contracts).
- Prefer extending existing modules over adding parallel abstractions for the same concern.
- Preserve API route style: validate entity existence first, return `HTTPException` with clear `detail`.
- For test execution changes, keep kind set compatible with current values:
  `unit`, `functional`, `api`, `perf_backend`, `perf_frontend`, `sec_backend`, `sec_frontend`, `ui`.
- Do not remove `skipped` behavior when tooling is missing; report reason via `detail`.
- Keep run lifecycle consistent: `pending -> running -> completed/failed`, and item status updates persisted per step.
- Reports must remain deterministic and readable: include summary table + stdout/stderr details.
- Keep backend as API-only service. For the root endpoint, return health/info JSON instead of server-side HTML rendering.
- Prefer minimal, additive changes; avoid broad refactors unless explicitly requested.
- After substantive edits, run at least one smoke check (`/docs` or backend import).
